{"data":"{\"stream\":true,\"stream_options\":{\"include_usage\":true},\"tools\":[{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Read text with one-based inclusive start_line/end_line. Optional max_bytes bounds the read; job reports cap inline output and preserve the full result on disk.\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"List immediate entries, sorted by name; directories end with /.\",\"name\":\"list_directory\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Search files recursively using a regular expression. context_lines defaults to zero. Output uses grep path:line:text and path-line-context with merged windows.\",\"name\":\"search_files\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"context_lines\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"pattern\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Write text, creating parent directories. Existing files require overwrite:true unless append:true. Append preserves existing content.\",\"name\":\"write_file\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"overwrite\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"append\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Replace one exact, unique old_text anchor with new_text. Zero or multiple matches refuse without changing the file; read and provide a more specific anchor.\",\"name\":\"edit_file\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"old_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"new_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"old_text\",\"new_text\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Start a fresh /bin/sh in a PTY. cwd applies only to this call, relative to the workspace. Merged output and exit_code stay on disk; a running report is a handle, not cancellation. ai_callback_delay is seconds (default 3); pattern matches unseen output; max_output_bytes defaults to 16384.\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"command\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Wait for a job, including a finished job. Return only unseen output; waiting does not stop execution.\",\"name\":\"wait_for_job\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Send a line of input to a running PTY job, then wait. A missing trailing newline is added.\",\"name\":\"send_input\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\",\"input\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Kill a job's process group. Go-only work is marked killed but its goroutine cannot be stopped.\",\"name\":\"kill_job\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Set one-shot wait/output limits for the very next call, whichever tool it is. That call reports consumption; explicit call arguments override these limits.\",\"name\":\"tool_limits\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Checkpoint at a completed micro-goal. Write text with what succeeded, what failed, source locations and next steps. Removes all tool traffic but preserves conversation and this note.\",\"name\":\"micro_handoff\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Keep the previous batch of tool results instead of automatic stubbing on supported models. Does not keep results of tools called alongside this call.\",\"name\":\"keep_tool_results\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}}},\"type\":\"function\"}],\"model\":\"gpt-4o-mini\",\"max_completion_tokens\":1024,\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You are a helpful assistant built from raw HTTP calls in Chapter 1 of The Art of Building AI Coding Agents. Answer briefly.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Memory 2026-10-11: In the Cedar Lantern project (CL-721), I decided against automatic deletion of imported notes to keep originals available for support when customers report mistakes. We archive source notes while storing accepted summaries separately, ensuring each summary retains a source identifier. Morgan will lead the archive review on October 18. An unresolved question is whether attachments should be in the same archive or separate. Notes have a default retention of thirty days, and originals must remain accessible for any failed summarization. \\n\\nInitially, I had coupled cleanup to the arrival of requests, but this could lead to the unintended deletion of unreviewed work due to unrelated requests. I shifted cleanup to occur after reviews, ensuring intact notes until the review process concludes. \\n\\nFor the Harbor Finch project (HF-934), scheduled for October 21 and owned by Priya, we rejected automatic retry of database migrations after timeouts due to risks from earlier commits. Instead, I will rely on a migration ledger to determine retry safety, requiring exact migration identifiers and measured errors from operators. An unresolved question remains about the ledger's location—within application data or a separate control database. Rollback packages will be available for seven days post-deployment. Evidence from logs indicated a worker stopped while the child process held the port open, prompting me to monitor child processes' resource impact more closely.\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Got it! Here's a summary of your notes from October 11, 2026:\\n\\n### Cedar Lantern Project (CL-721)\\n- **Note Management**: Decided against automatic deletion of imported notes to maintain originals for customer support. Original notes will be archived, while accepted summaries will be stored separately with source identifiers.\\n- **Archive Review**: Morgan will lead the review on October 18.\\n- **Attachments Question**: Unresolved issue regarding whether to archive attachments with notes or separately.\\n- **Retention Policy**: Default retention for notes is thirty days, keeping originals accessible for failed summarizations.\\n- **Cleanup Process**: Transitioned cleanup to occur after reviews to avoid accidental deletion of unreviewed work.\\n\\n### Harbor Finch Project (HF-934)\\n- **Scheduled Review**: Scheduled for October 21 and owned by Priya.\\n- **Database Migrations**: Automatic retries after timeouts were rejected due to risks. Instead, a migration ledger will track retry safety using exact migration identifiers and operator-reported errors.\\n- **Ledger Location Question**: Still undecided if the ledger should be part of application data or in a separate control database.\\n- **Rollback Policy**: Rollback packages available for seven days post-deployment.\\n- **Monitoring Child Processes**: Noted the need to monitor child processes more closely after an issue with a worker holding a port open during a stop.\\n\\nLet me know if you need any further assistance!\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Without using tools, recall both project names, diagnostic codes, owners, dates, rejected approaches and reasons. Explicitly identify the two unresolved questions. Do not invent a resolved answer.\"}]}","event":"request"}
